# Day 11: Apex Testing Framework & Asynchronous Processing

Welcome to the Day 11 project repository! This module bridges the gap between high-performance backend processing and platform stability. It covers the core strategies required to write robust unit tests and design scalable asynchronous architectures within the Salesforce multi-tenant environment.

---

## 🧪 Why Testing Matters

Testing on the Salesforce platform isn't just a requirement to bypass deployment blocks; it is a foundational pillar of enterprise application health. 

* **Enforcing Platform Stability:** Salesforce strictly requires an overall minimum of **75% code coverage** to deploy Apex code into a production environment. 
* **Regression Prevention:** A comprehensive test suite acts as an automated safety net. It ensures that future modifications, updates, or Salesforce seasonal releases do not break existing business logic.
* **Code as Documentation:** Well-written unit tests serve as executable documentation. They clearly illustrate to other developers the expected inputs, boundaries, and outputs of any given Apex method.
* **Bulk Verification:** Testing forces developers to validate how custom code handles hundreds of records simultaneously, catching efficiency bugs before real-time users encounter production exceptions.

