## 💼 Async Use Cases

Salesforce provides four core asynchronous tools, each optimized for distinct engineering challenges:

| Asynchronous Tool | Primary Use Case | Key Features & Constraints |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Future Methods (`@future`)** | Quick background tasks and isolating callouts from standard transactional logic. | Accepts only primitive data types (or collections of primitives); cannot chain multiple future jobs together. |
| **Queueable Apex** | Complex background processing requiring state tracking and relational tracking. | Accepts complex data types (objects, custom classes); supports **job chaining** to run tasks sequentially. |
| **Batch Apex** | Large-scale data scrubbing, archiving, or processing across millions of records. | Splits massive record sets into manageable chunks (default 200 per batch); runs across separate start, execute, and finish phases. |
| **Scheduled Apex** | Running specific execution scripts automatically at defined times or intervals. | Uses a powerful cron expression engine to run logic daily, weekly, or monthly (e.g., generating weekly performance summaries). |

