## 🛡️ Reliability Discussion

Building asynchronous architecture requires strict defensive coding practices due to shared cloud infrastructure. To ensure long-term system reliability, the following patterns are built into this repository:

### 1. Designing for Governor Limits
Asynchronous processes receive higher governor limits than synchronous transactions (e.g., heap size is doubled to 12MB, and maximum SOQL queries increase from 100 to 200). However, because these limits are still strictly enforced per background chunk, all collection data paths must remain thoroughly bulkified.

### 2. Testing Asynchronous Blocks
Because async tasks execute whenever resources are free, unit tests cannot natively track them. To handle this, we use platform boundaries:
